# Shell scripts and systemd unit files must always have LF line endings —
# they run/get parsed on the Linux production server, and a CRLF shebang
# line ("#!/bin/bash\r") fails with a "bad interpreter" error there,
# regardless of local core.autocrlf settings.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.path text eol=lf
*.service text eol=lf
